> > On my alpha, the kernel reports the following abaout clamd in the syslo=
g:

> > Jan  6 16:38:07 ente kernel: clamd(27863): unaligned trap at=20
> > 0000020000037750: 00000200012fecf2 28 0

> This means, that clamd tried to access some memory which the CPU
> cannot directly access, because the address is not properly aligned.
> The kernel fixes that, and then the access occurs. So this message is
> harmless, except that it costs you a little performance.=20

> > I find those records several times a day. What does this mean? Do I hav=
e=20
> > to file a bug?

